WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:04.730
So when you hear the word "marketing," what
do you think about?

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:08.780
Really, marketing, because the world of business
is a lot about marketing, right?

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:11.960
How you market yourself, your product, what
do you think about?

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.270
What word comes to mind?

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:19.080
See, for me when I think about the word marketing,
I think about how you tell your story.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:23.370
How you tell the story of your company, how
you tell the story of yourself, how your story's

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:24.660
being told.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.740
Is it reaching the audience you want it to
reach?

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:29.290
Do you know the audience that you want to
reach?

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:30.539
That's marketing.

00:00:30.539 --> 00:00:35.690
And a lot of times - I remember one time I
was in an audience and I heard this speaker

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:41.399
speaking from stage, and this audience was
filled with 70-year-olds who are getting ready

00:00:41.399 --> 00:00:42.399
to retire.

00:00:42.399 --> 00:00:43.800
They were between 70 -80.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.399
And he's on stage.

00:00:45.399 --> 00:00:47.940
No one in the audience is less than 55.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:52.059
And he's on stage and saying, "Can you imagine
if one day you're driving a Ferrari?

00:00:52.059 --> 00:00:53.909
Can you imagine if one day you're driving
a Lamborghini?

00:00:53.909 --> 00:00:57.020
Can you imagine if one day you're going down
to the beach and you're surfing?

00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:01.749
And I'm sitting there saying, "Does he know
who he's marketing to and how he's telling

00:01:01.749 --> 00:01:02.749
the story?"

00:01:02.749 --> 00:01:05.240
Because your story doesn't resonate with this
audience.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:08.190
Maybe it resonated with a different one, but
it doesn't resonate with this audience.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:12.790
So, it is very, very important for you to
study marketing, and marketing becomes an

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:13.790
art.

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:15.130
It becomes a lot of fun if you learn how to
do it the proper way.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:16.130
It helps you out in business.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:17.520
It helps you out in every aspect of your life.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:23.150
So many of you kept asking me, Pat, give me
top books I need to read on marketing.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:24.560
And finally, we're giving it to you.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:28.230
And I'm giving it to you in a way where I'll
recommend 10 books to you, and then from there

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:29.840
you can do whatever you want with these 10
books.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:34.390
I believe every entrepreneur must study these
10 books for marketing.

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:38.900
#10: for me on this list would be The Art
of SEO.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:43.100
The Art of SEO is #10 on the list and the
reason why this book - now keep in mind, you

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.900
can buy this book and I think they have the
most recent edition out now.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:49.180
I don't think this is even the most recent
one.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:52.310
(Mario, I think there's another edition after
this one.

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:54.390
Yeah, there's another edition after this one.)

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.220
The Art of SEO.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:58.170
And it's pretty big.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:01.000
You're talking about 645 pages.

